{"id":48,"text":"One cold January morning, a man in jeans and a baseball cap stood in a busy subway station. He took a violin out of its case and began to play.\n\nHe played for forty-five minutes. Over a thousand people passed him on their way to work. Most of them didn’t even look at him. Only six people stopped for a moment, and he earned about thirty-two dollars.\n\nNobody knew that the violinist was one of the greatest musicians in the world. Two days earlier, he had played in a famous concert hall, where the tickets cost hundreds of dollars. The violin in his hands was worth millions.\n\nA newspaper had organised the experiment to ask an important question: “Do we notice beauty when it appears in an unexpected place?”\n\nOnly one person recognised the music. She was a woman who had once heard him in a concert. She stood still, listening, with tears in her eyes.\n\nWhen the experiment ended, a journalist asked her, “Why did you stop?”\n\n“Because I couldn’t walk away,” she said. “How can the rest of us walk past something so wonderful?”\n\nMoral: Beauty and wonder are everywhere, but we have to slow down to see them.","tr":null,"gl":{"one":"один","cold":"холодный","january":"январь","morning":"утро","a":"(неопределённый артикль)","man":"человек, мужчина","in":"в","jeans":"джинсы","and":"и","baseball":"бейсбол","cap":"кепка; крышка","stood":"стоял","busy":"занятой","subway":"метро","station":"станция","he":"он","took":"взял","violin":"скрипка","out":"наружу","of":"из; (родительный падеж)","its":"его (для предмета)","case":"случай; футляр","began":"начал","to":"к, в; чтобы","play":"играть","played":"играл","for":"для; в течение","forty":"сорок","five":"пять","minutes":"минуты","over":"над; кончилось; на протяжении","thousand":"тысяча","people":"люди","passed":"прошёл","him":"его, ему","on":"на","their":"их","way":"путь; способ","work":"работать; работа","most":"самый","them":"их, им","didn't":"не (сделал)","even":"даже","look":"смотреть","at":"в, у, на","only":"т